## 1. Component graph

The envelope schema is a **single file, one `$id`, three referenceable subschemas**. It is the
root contract of SAKG-1: four downstream backlog nodes `$ref` it and none of them may restate
its field set.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph FILE["sakg/schema/envelope.schema.json — $id: sakg://schema/envelope/v1.0.0"]
        ROOT["ROOT = stored envelope<br/>(the node as the graph holds it)"]
        ING["$defs/ingest_envelope<br/>$anchor: ingest-envelope<br/>(what a producer may emit)"]
        CORE["$defs/envelope_core<br/>(all §4.2 fields, shapes + ranges)"]
        PRIM["$defs/ — node_id · node_type · namespace · timestamp<br/>sha256 · origin_ref · evidence_ref_id<br/>facets · coordinates · status · confidence"]
        STATE["$defs/state_invariants<br/>(allOf of 4 if/then blocks, one per status)"]
    end

    CORE --> PRIM
    ROOT -->|allOf| CORE
    ROOT -->|allOf| STATE
    ING  -->|allOf| CORE
    ING  -->|"not: required[confidence]"| CORE
    ING  -->|"const: status = candidate"| CORE

    subgraph FIX["tests/sakg/fixtures/envelope/"]
        MAN["MANIFEST.json — fixture → {profile, verdict, clause, expected keyword+path}"]
        VAL["valid/*.json  (15)"]
        INV["invalid/*.json (15)"]
    end

    TEST["tests/sakg/test_envelope_schema.py"]
    TEST --> FILE
    TEST --> MAN
    MAN --> VAL
    MAN --> INV

    BUNDLE["F-BUNDLE — bundle.schema.json"] -->|"$ref #ingest-envelope"| ING
    STORE["I-STORE — sakg/store.py"] -->|"validates writes vs ROOT"| ROOT
    INGEST["I-INGEST — sakg/ingest.py"] -->|"validates reads vs #ingest-envelope"| ING
    PROJ["F-PROJ — projection.schema.json"] -->|"node_summary $refs label+summary+id"| CORE
```

**Placement rationale.**

- **One file, not three.** `envelope.schema.json` is named by the accept command (`json.loads`
  on exactly that path). Splitting profiles across files would force `$ref` resolution across
  file boundaries in every consumer and give three things to version instead of one.
- **Root = stored envelope.** §4.2 describes the node *as the graph holds it* (`confidence` is
  present and derived). Making the root the stored form means a naive `validate(doc, schema)`
  by any future consumer checks the strongest form. The ingest profile is the deliberate
  relaxation, reached only by explicit `$ref`.
- **`MANIFEST.json` sits at `fixtures/envelope/`, not inside `valid/` or `invalid/`.** The
  accept commands glob `valid/*.json` and `invalid/*.json`; a manifest inside either directory
  would inflate those counts with a non-fixture. Placement is load-bearing, not cosmetic.
- **No orphan:** every `$defs` entry in §2.2 is reached from `ROOT` or `#ingest-envelope`;
  every fixture is reached from `MANIFEST.json`; the test asserts both directions (§6.4).

